; A Petri net: a producer makes two items into a buffer of two free slots, and
; a consumer uses them.  Places are rows; a transition takes and makes tokens.
; Every run ends with both items used and the slots free again.
(step one)
(ready) (ready)
(slot) (slot)
(rule produce (take (ready) (slot)) (make (item)))
(rule consume (take (item)) (make (used) (slot)))
